// Base 64, RFC 4648, in the two moods this library needs it in:
// https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4648
//
// The header and the stanza bodies want the unpadded alphabet with the
// canonical-encoding rule of RFC 4648 §3.5 enforced on the way in; the ASCII
// armor wants the padded alphabet of §4. Both directions must be exact: a
// decoder that accepts a second spelling of the same bytes lets two different
// files carry the same header MAC, and every test vector that pins an encoding
// would still pass.
//
// Not here: the URL and filename alphabets, which the format does not use.
import {
  "moonbitlang/core/buffer",
}
